<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#808080;">Step: 47 (<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Final result</span>):</span><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">think</span>&gt;<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To determine which statement is false, letś analyze each option:</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1. “The differential diagnosis on this case is remote injury vs. is remote contusion.”</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is <span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">false</span> because the image clearly shows a distant regional contusion, not a distant infarct.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2. “There is a well developed gliotic wall associated with this remote injury.”</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is <span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">true</span> because a well developed gliotic wall is a clear feature in the image.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3. “The presence of macrophages is not helpful in distinguishing this from a subacute process.”</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is <span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">true</span> because the presence of macrophages in subacute processes is a characteristic feature of subacute processes.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4. “This is very unlikely to have resulted from venous occlusion.”</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">This is <span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.11.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">true</span> because the image clearly shows a distant infarct, not venous occlusion.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, the false statement is option <span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.12.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">A</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">/think</span>&gt;<span id="A3.p3.pic1.p19.13.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
